      "item_id": "54d0748b-24cd-4172-ac74-5b338aa5c5bc",
      "summary": "The FDA issued a warning letter to El Gordo Spices, LLC following an inspection of its seafood and spice repacking facility. The firm was cited for serious violations of Seafood HACCP regulations for its dried shrimp products, including failing to identify shrimp allergens as a hazard and failing to implement corrective actions for sulfiting agents. Additionally, multiple products, including dried shrimp, spices, sesame seeds, and textured soy, were found to be misbranded for failing to include Nutrition Facts panels, not providing complete bilingual labeling, and not declaring the color additive FD&C Red No. 40 Lake in ground shrimp.",
      "key_regulations": [
        "21 CFR Part 123",
        "21 CFR Part 101",
        "21 U.S.C. § 342(a)(4)",
